<title>USA: Goodyear, union say talks to resume Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Goodyear, union say talks to resume Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goodyear Tire and Rubber Co and the United Steelworkers of America said contract talks covering nearly 13,000 striking Goodyear workers adjourned Monday evening and are scheduled to resume Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>Spokesmen for the giant tiremaker and the union said the talks would resume at a neutral site in Cincinnati where discussion have been going on for more than two months.</p>
<p>The workers struck early Sunday after negotiators were unable to reach agreement on a new three-year contract.</p>
<p>The striking workers are employed at nine Goodyear plants in Ohio, Alabama, Nebraska, Kansas, Virginia, Tennessee and Wisconsin.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
